# HAOS Apps repository

Multi-app Home Assistant repository: `github.com/byte-bridge/haos-apps`.

Target **Home Assistant OS** only. See [docs/HOME_ASSISTANT_ADRS.md](docs/HOME_ASSISTANT_ADRS.md). Supervised was dropped in [discussion #1198](https://github.com/home-assistant/architecture/discussions/1198); [ADR-0013 Container](https://github.com/home-assistant/architecture/blob/master/adr/0013-home-assistant-container.md) has no Supervisor/apps.

## Structure

- App folders at the **repo root** (e.g. `rancher/`), each with `config.yaml` and `AGENTS.md`
- `repository.yaml` registers the repo with Home Assistant
- `templates/app/` scaffold — copy it; includes a starter `AGENTS.md`
- Shared docs in `docs/`
- Cursor: root `AGENTS.md` + nested `<slug>/AGENTS.md` + `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` ([docs](https://cursor.com/docs/rules))

## When adding or editing an app

1. Read root `AGENTS.md`, the app’s `AGENTS.md` (if present), and `docs/ADDING_AN_APP.md`
2. Follow [HA app configuration](https://developers.home-assistant.io/docs/apps/configuration)
3. Use [home-assistant/apps-example](https://github.com/home-assistant/apps-example) for packaging/layout/CI; use each app’s `AGENTS.md` for runtime pattern
4. Shell scripts: `#!/usr/bin/with-contenv bashio`, LF line endings
5. Update the apps table in root `README.md`
6. Document security (Protection mode, privileged access) in that app’s `DOCS.md`
7. For versioned app changes: update `<slug>/CHANGELOG.md` first; that entry is the git commit message

## Code style

- Minimal, focused diffs — one app per change when possible
- Match the pattern documented in that app’s `AGENTS.md`
- Don't pin Alpine package versions unless required
- Don't commit secrets or create git commits unless asked
